      "speaker": null,
      "text": "MOOD: THE OPTATIVES",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 5,
      "bbox": [
        323,
        184,
        401,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": 183,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Most of the verbs you have met so far have been in one of two ‘moods’: the indicative or the imperative. The ‘mood’ of a verb gives important clues as to its function in a sentence:",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        408,
        186,
        452,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The indicative mood, for example, is generally used to make statements or ask questions.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "bullet",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        455,
        186,
        477,
        665
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The imperative mood is used to give orders.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "bullet",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        486,
        186,
        532,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "There are two further moods in Greek: the optative and the subjunctive.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "arrow",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        526,
        237,
        616,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Here you encounter the optative (and you can fight over whether to stress the ‘o’ or the ‘a’). You will meet a number of uses of this mood in future sections, but as you will discover, most examples of the optative in Greek require the use of words like ‘would’, ‘could’ and ‘might’ when translating in English.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        643,
        186,
        658,
        535
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Present optative active and middle",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
